(a) Ferecetotherium kelloggi, the oldest sperm whale in the world and the oldest member of a living group of whales; 
(b) Oligodelphis azebajdzanicus, possibly, the oldest dolphin in the world; 
(c) Kelloggia barbarus, a shark-toothed whale with one of the most complete skeletons; 
(d) Imerocetus karaganicus and Otradnocetus virodovi, the oldest baleen whales from Europe; 
(e) Iniopsis caucasica and Kharthlidelphis diceros, the dolphins of uncertain phylogenetic affinities.

